// Title: Lazarus "Operation Dream Job" - libmupdf.dll Side-Loading
// Description: Detects the DLL side-loading chain used by Lazarus Group's
//   Operation Dream Job campaign (exploiting CVE-2026-68820). Victims are
//   lured via fake recruiter job offers on LinkedIn into downloading an
//   encrypted archive that side-loads a malicious "libmupdf.dll" to launch
//   the MISTPEN downloader while displaying a decoy job description. A
//   legitimate libmupdf.dll normally ships inside a PDF viewer's Program
//   Files install directory, not a user-writable path.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1566.002 (Phishing: Spearphishing Link), T1204.002 (User
//   Execution: Malicious File), T1574.002 (Hijack Execution Flow: DLL
//   Side-Loading)
// Data source: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (DeviceImageLoadEvents)
// False positives: Rare - flag if an org has a legitimate custom PDF tool
//   named libmupdf.dll deployed from a non-standard path; verify the
//   InitiatingProcess and SHA256 against known-good baselines before
//   dismissing.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FileName =~ "libmupdf.dll"
| where FolderPath !startswith @"C:\Program Files"
    and FolderPath !startswith @"C:\Program Files (x86)"
    and FolderPath !startswith @"C:\Windows"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, FileName, FolderPath, SHA256,
    InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessSHA256,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName
| order by Timestamp desc
